.TH pvc-ratechanger 1  "pvc-ratechanger " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-ratechanger \- Resample at a variable rate (varispeed)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-ratechanger\fR [\fB\-\-synthesis\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-table\-lookup\fR] [\fB\-\-pi\-interpolation\-points\fR] [\fB\-\-truncation\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-synthesize\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-channel\fR] [\fB\-\-normalize\fR] [\fB\-\-time\-origin\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-semitones\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-semitones\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-low\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-high\fR] [\fB\-\-new\-sample\-rate\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Varispeed resampler: reads raw audio directly (no `.pva` analysis file first) and resynthesizes it at a possibly time\-varying playback rate and/or semitone shift, via windowed\-sinc summation, sample\-and\-hold/decimation, or linear interpolation.
.PP
Ports `ratechanger` (`legacy/pvc_src/ratechanger.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools::ratechanger`\*(Aqs doc comment for what\*(Aqs in and out of scope, including a real, verified heap\-buffer\-overflow in the C\*(Aqs own default sinc\-table lookup (confirmed under ASan \- safely clamped here instead of reproduced).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-synthesis\-mode\fR \fI<SYNTHESIS_MODE>\fR [default: sinc]
`\-X`: per\-sample synthesis method
.TP
\fB\-\-table\-lookup\fR \fI<TABLE_LOOKUP>\fR [default: on]
`\-t`: use the Blackman\-windowed sinc lookup table (fast) instead of computing `sin`/`cos` directly (slow). Only affects `\-\-synthesis\-mode sinc`
.TP
\fB\-\-pi\-interpolation\-points\fR \fI<PI_INTERPOLATION_POINTS>\fR [default: 100]
`\-L`: lookup\-table interpolation points per sinc period
.TP
\fB\-\-truncation\-db\fR \fI<TRUNCATION_DB>\fR [default: \-60]
`\-B`: sinc window truncation level in dB (must be `< 0`; typically `\-30` to `\-96`)
.TP
\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 0]
`\-d`: output duration in seconds. `0` (the default) triggers output\-duration synthesis regardless of `\-\-synthesize\-duration`, matching the C\*(Aqs own `if (outputDuration <= 0.) synthesizeOutputDuration = true;`
.TP
\fB\-\-synthesize\-duration\fR
`\-D`: search for an output duration that synchronizes the completion of the rate\-change control functions with the end of the output, via an iterative convergence algorithm (see `pvc_core::tools::ratechanger::resolve_output_duration`). Always on when `\-\-duration` is `0` or unset, regardless of this flag
.TP
\fB\-\-channel\fR \fI<CHANNEL>\fR [default: 0]
`\-C`: input channel to process, `1`\-based. `0` (the default) processes every input channel
.TP
\fB\-\-normalize\fR \fI<NORMALIZE>\fR [default: input]
`\-n`: post\-synthesis normalization
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-origin\fR \fI<TIME_ORIGIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-O`: source time\-position origin in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\-in\fR \fI<RATE_IN>\fR [default: 1]
`\-r`: rate multiplier as a function of *input* sound time \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\-out\fR \fI<RATE_OUT>\fR [default: 1]
`\-R`: rate multiplier as a function of *output* sound time \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-semitones\-in\fR \fI<SEMITONES_IN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-s`: semitone pitch shift as a function of *input* sound time \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-semitones\-out\fR \fI<SEMITONES_OUT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-S`: semitone pitch shift as a function of *output* sound time \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\-in\fR \fI<GAIN_IN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-a`: amplitude envelope in dB as a function of *input* sound time \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\-out\fR \fI<GAIN_OUT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-A`: amplitude envelope in dB as a function of *output* sound time \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-low\fR \fI<WINDOW_LOW>\fR [default: 0]
`\-b`: input time window low boundary in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-high\fR \fI<WINDOW_HIGH>\fR [default: \-1]
`\-e`: input time window high boundary in seconds (`<= 0` = end of input) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-sample\-rate\fR \fI<NEW_SAMPLE_RATE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-m`: impose a new sample rate on the output header (`<= 0`, the default, keeps the input\*(Aqs own sample rate). Does not itself resample \- only changes the output file\*(Aqs declared rate
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

